VERDICT
============================================================================================
    beta-only fitted: (A) authority   7.4 dB PASS   (B) direction FAIL   (C) ramp rms 3.88 -> 6.20 FAIL
    physical clipper: (A) authority   1.2 dB FAIL   (B) direction FAIL   (C) ramp rms 13.97 -> 14.60 FAIL

  ** GATE NOT PASSED. ** The step-1 measurement stands on its own (it is a direct,
  bleed-free, self-tested measurement of a circuit quantity, and the shipped power law
  is demonstrably wrong), but the claim that reshaping it CLOSES the noon H3-H2 gap is
  NOT supported. Do not present a C-taper as the noon fix.
  Specifically (B): the real pedal is QUIETER at noon than the model, while noon
  H3-H2 RISES with level and the model is already SHORT there — so the corrected
  taper moves noon the WRONG WAY. The noon deficit must come from somewhere else
  (next suspect per §3u.6: the clipper INPUT coupling — GRUNT cap bank + R16 —
  for drive-dependent behaviour a memoryless VTC cannot produce).
